<title>UK: Eurobonds - Expected emerging market redemptions.</title>
<headline>Eurobonds - Expected emerging market redemptions.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a summary by region of expected emerging market international bond redemptions, including Yankee bonds, throughout 1997.</p>
<p>The list was compiled from Capital DATA Bondware data. All figures are millions of dollars, except monthly totals.</p>
<p>		    JAN  FEB  MAR  APR  MAY  JUN  JUL  AUG  SEP  OCT NOV DEC TOTAL</p>
<p>AFRICA		0  315    0  210   73    0    0    0    0    0   0   0  598</p>
<p>EASTERN EUROPE   21  216  178    0    0  124    0  197    0  324   76 110 1246</p>
<p>FAR EAST	   76  660  747  794  413  456  711 1070  667 1232  400 1001 8227</p>
<p>INDIAN SUB</p>
<p>CONTINENT	   0  150  190    0    0    0  149    0    0    0    0 100 589</p>
<p>LATIN AMERICA   882 265 1180  614  550 2246 2372  755  460 1637 2413 2291 15665</p>
<p>MIDDLE EAST	 0    0  615  232    0  392   30  200    0  400 413    0  2283</p>
<p>OTHER	     100    0   73    0    0  325   50  534    0  210  80  540 1912</p>
<p>TOTAL (bln)     1.1  1.6  3.0  1.9  1.0  3.5  3.3  2.8  1.1  3.8 3.4  4.0 30.5</p>
<p>There is a total of $30.5 billion emerging market issue bond redemptions expected in 1997. This compares with $22.9 billion redemptions in 1996 and an expected $38.2 billion in 1998.</p>
